            <div xml:id="d380">

                <pb facs="0486" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg384"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5174: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Munro</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-12-05T09:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">December 5,
                                1927—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 12:40
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>363. Department’s November 29, 8 p.m., next to last paragraph. As a permanent
                    arrangement I consider it preferable that the electoral machinery should be
                    reorganized just before each Presidential election as under the present law. The
                    law might however be <pb facs="0487" n="385" xml:id="pg385"/> amended to make
                    the terms of members of the electoral boards 2 years so that these boards would
                    again be reorganized before each congressional election on the basis of the
                    results of the preceding election.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Munro</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
